The tests write to their own temporary directory and to a per-run folder on
the USB volume, never to C:\MerchandisingBackups or the operational off-host
folder. The retention test exists to prove deletion works, so pointing it at
the real backup directory would have made it capable of deleting real backups.


SECTION 8 — WHAT THIS DOES NOT PROVE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
That the dump RESTORES. Spec section 15's "Verification" control requires a
restore against an isolated database or a controlled maintenance window, and
that is P1-18, not this card. What is proven here is that the dump is
complete: mysqldump's trailing "-- Dump completed" marker is checked in
production code, not only in the test, because exit code 0 plus a non-empty
file does not rule out a truncated dump from a full disk or a killed process.

The Task Scheduler job was triggered manually rather than waited on for a
day. See p1-17-scheduled-task.log.
